**Update `availablePlans` when the list is loaded.**

After creation, `setSecurityPlan` makes the new SSP active. If the selector previously loaded an empty list, `availablePlans` remains empty, so the selector still shows `No systems yet`. The selector displays the active SSP through its fallback option, so the new SSP remains visible. However, `select()` cannot resolve that fallback option because it searches only `availablePlans`.

`NoActiveSystem` is not shown on `system:overview` in this state. `SystemView` checks `!systemSecurityPlan`, and the new active SSP satisfies that guard.

Append the plan only when `availablePlansLoaded` is already true. Do not call `setAvailablePlans` before the list loads, because that marks a local partial list as complete.

<details>
<summary>Suggested fix</summary>

```diff
+    if (systemStore.availablePlansLoaded) {
+      systemStore.setAvailablePlans([
+        ...systemStore.availablePlans,
+        data.value!,
+      ]);
+    }
     systemStore.setSecurityPlan(data.value!);
```

</details>

